      "problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\left( 5(\\sqrt{x})^{3} - 4 x^2 + 5\\right) \\,\\textrm d x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5(\\sqrt{x})^{3}-4{x}^{2}+5)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5{x}^{3/2}-4{x}^{2}+5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int {x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int {x}^{2}\\text{d}x+5\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5(\\frac{{x}^{5/2}}{\\frac{5}{2}})-4(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})+5(x)+C \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}+5x+C \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}+5x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
